; WHEN the declaration width budget is counted, pinned by a case whose
; answer changes with it.
;
; `401-decl-macro-size-limit` pins THAT `expMaxDecls` refuses. It could
; not see when, because it crosses the limit and stops either way. This
; case crosses the same limit in the same shape and then asks the
; template for one more declaration that cannot be built - so the two
; orders give two different diagnostics, and the golden is the answer.
;
; `expInstantiateDecl` used to add `(vecLen made)` to the running total
; AFTER `expBuildDecls` returned, which is two defects in one line.
;
;   * The count moved once per INSTANTIATION, so nothing bounded what a
;     single one built. A declaration-position `syntax/for` NESTS
;     (macro-system.md: "nested iterations compose"), so one invocation
;     builds a PRODUCT, and the allocator is a bump allocator with no
;     free. Measured on this tree with `axiom check`, on a two-level
;     nest whose product is exact: 12,000 declarations reached 11 MB,
;     40,000 reached 32 MB, 200,000 reached 153 MB, 800,000 reached
;     604 MB - each of them printing "more than the limit of 10000"
;     only after the whole product was in memory - and 3,200,000
;     reached 2 GB in 1.27 s and was killed by the cap with no
;     diagnostic and no output at all. A three-level nest of 200x200x200
;     is 16,000,000 declarations and died the same way in 1.96 s. That
;     is the failure AX3024's long form says this number exists to
;     prevent, reproduced with the number in place. Counted per push,
;     every one of those refuses in 0.04 s and under 12 MB.
;
;   * `(vecLen made)` was reached only `(if (!= made 0))`, and a
;     template that REFUSES answers 0 - so a fan-out followed by any
;     refusing form was never counted at all. That is what this file
;     is. `nm` is bound to the literal `7`, and a generated
;     declaration's name must be a bare identifier (AX3027), so the
;     6,400 pairs above it went to the allocator and contributed
;     nothing to a budget that had already been passed by 2,800.
;
; So the golden here READ `AX3027` before the count moved inside the
; build, and reads `AX3024` after it: the budget is crossed at
; declaration 10,001, and the form that cannot be built is never
; reached. Revert the counting site and this file says AX3027 again.
;
; 80 x 80 pairs is 401's size and for 401's reason - it crosses 10,000
; from ONE invocation, so the refusal carries one expansion frame
; rather than thousands. It is deliberately NOT sized to the millions
; measured above: a fixture that only fails by exhausting the machine
; is a gate that takes the machine with it.
(data Wide
  (K0)
